"margin": 8.79, "lean": 3.0, "environment": 4.15, "incumbency": 0.0, "money": 1.64}, "rating_margin": 12.43, "sigma_race": 5.5, "sigma_total": 5.9, "baseline_margin": 9.2, "analyst_adjustment": -1.7, "key_factors": ["Haaland leads recent independent polls by 6-7 points", "Fundraising edge of roughly 20-to-1 for Haaland", "All seven analyst ratings favor Democrats; markets price ~90%+ for Haaland", "Open seat in a state leaning Democratic by about 4 points"], "rationale": "Recent independent polls show Haaland ahead by six to seven points, her fundraising advantage over Hull is roughly twenty-to-one, and analysts uniformly place the open seat on the Democratic side; prediction markets price her near ninety percent, supporting a Likely Democratic rating with a mid-single-digit expected margin.", "watch": "A late shift in the national political environment toward Republicans, or undecided voters breaking heavily to Hull, could narrow the race toward toss-up territory.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Michelle Lujan Grisham (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "New Mexico's open governor's race pits Democratic nominee Deb Haaland against Republican Gregg Hull to succeed term-limited Governor Michelle Lujan Grisham. The state leans Democratic by about four points, and Haaland has led every independent poll this fall, most recently by six to seven points. She has also raised more than twenty times what Hull has collected, giving her a dominant advertising position in the final weeks.\n\nAnalysts rate the contest from Lean Democratic to Solid Democratic, with most calling it Likely Democratic, and prediction markets put her odds around ninety percent or better. Barack Obama and Michigan Governor Gretchen Whitmer have campaigned for Haaland, who has centered her message on affordability, while Hull has pledged transparency at the state child-welfare agency. The main question is whether the final margin lands in the mid-single digits, as polls suggest, or somewhat higher given the state's Democratic lean.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9664, "margin": 10.58}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9571, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9605, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.948, "margin": 10.2}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9415, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9502, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9552, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9463, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9506, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9559, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9507, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9606, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9549, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9273, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9256, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9234, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9241, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9268, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.923, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.9163, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.9397, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.9351, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.9301, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-15", "p_dem": 0.9278, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-16", "p_dem": 0.9324, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-17", "p_dem": 0.9268, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-18", "p_dem": 0.9253, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-19", "p_dem": 0.9041, "margin": 7.5}]}